WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:08.665
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:16.575
Unit three: Listening: Multiple Choice and Maps. Today you will choose the best answer and follow directions on a map.

4
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.574
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:23.940
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.668
Option.

7
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:29.101
Option means one of the possible answers.

8
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:31.333
Option B is correct.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.708
Your turn. Say: Option.

10
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.417
Option.

11
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.266
Distractor.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.260
Distractor means a wrong answer that sounds possible.

13
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.629
One option is a distractor.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:50.032
Your turn. Say: Distractor.

15
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:54.100
Distractor.

16
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.037
Paraphrase.

17
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.687
Paraphrase means to say the same idea in different words.

18
00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:03.236
The speaker paraphrases the question.

19
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.398
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

20
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:10.339
Paraphrase.

21
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:11.980
Opposite.

22
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:15.865
Opposite means facing something across a space.

23
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.310
The bank is opposite the park.

24
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:21.581
Your turn. Say: Opposite.

25
00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:25.504
Opposite.

26
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.193
Next to.

27
00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:29.893
Next to means beside.

28
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:32.471
The library is next to the cafe.

29
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:35.434
Your turn. Say: Next to.

30
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.498
Next to.

31
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.030
Junction.

32
00:01:42.017 --> 00:01:44.481
Junction means a place where roads meet.

33
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:46.677
Turn left at the junction.

34
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.854
Your turn. Say: Junction.

35
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.562
Junction.

36
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:55.190
Label.

37
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:59.274
Label means to write a name on a map or diagram.

38
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:01.744
Label the buildings on the map.

39
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.666
Your turn. Say: Label.

40
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.385
Label.

41
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.070
Direction.

42
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:14.012
Direction means the way something is facing or going.

43
00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:16.384
Follow the directions carefully.

44
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:19.473
Your turn. Say: Direction.

45
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:23.276
Direction.

46
00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:28.252
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.117 --> 00:02:31.848
Visal, what makes multiple choice difficult?

48
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:43.996
The speaker often mentions all three options, but only one answers the question. The other options are distractors, so you must listen to the whole idea.

49
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:47.373
How do the questions use different words?

50
00:02:48.483 --> 00:02:59.623
The question paraphrases the audio. If the question says expensive, the speaker may say it costs more than we expected, so you listen for meaning, not matching words.

51
00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:02.159
And map questions?

52
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:14.935
Find the starting point first, then follow the directions step by step. Words like opposite, next to, behind and at the junction show where each building is.

53
00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.763
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:23.321
Grammar focus: Strategy: listen for meaning, not just words.

55
00:03:23.621 --> 00:03:24.936
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.194
The speaker mentions all options, but only one answers the question.

57
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:34.463
Start at the entrance, turn left at the junction, and the cafe is opposite the park.

58
00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:43.544
For multiple choice, underline the key idea in the question and listen for a paraphrase. For maps, locate the start and follow each direction in order.

59
00:03:44.283 --> 00:03:48.399
Be careful! Don't say: I choose the first option I hear.

60
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.716
Say: I wait for the whole idea.

61
00:03:53.016 --> 00:03:54.749
Beware of distractors.

62
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:57.965
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.244
The Campus Tour.

64
00:04:00.544 --> 00:04:03.414
A guide shows new students around campus.

65
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.360
She says the library was once planned for the north side, but it is now next to the cafe.

66
00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:13.434
To reach the sports hall, turn right at the junction.

67
00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:17.106
The hall is opposite the pool, not behind it.

68
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.365
Students must choose the sentence that matches the final route.

69
00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:26.538
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:28.907
A distractor is blank.

71
00:04:29.207 --> 00:04:34.532
A, a wrong but tempting answer. B, the correct answer. C, a map symbol.

72
00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:41.123
The answer is A: a wrong but tempting answer.

73
00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:47.153
The speaker says: it costs more than we expected. The question word is probably blank.

74
00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:50.840
A, free. B, expensive. C, cheap.

75
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.992
The answer is B: expensive.

76
00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.231
First on a map question you blank.

77
00:05:00.531 --> 00:05:04.660
A, guess. B, skip it. C, find the starting point.

78
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.792
The answer is C: find the starting point.

79
00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.938
The sports hall is blank the pool.

80
00:05:14.238 --> 00:05:17.555
A, opposite. B, behind. C, inside.

81
00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.088
The answer is A: opposite.

82
00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.784
According to the guide, where is the library now?

83
00:05:27.084 --> 00:05:31.828
A, behind the hall. B, next to the cafe. C, north side.

84
00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:38.016
The answer is B: next to the cafe.

85
00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.514
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.557
How do you avoid distractors in multiple choice questions?

87
00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.885
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:57.185 --> 00:06:16.617
I read the question and underline the key idea before the audio starts. When I listen, I expect paraphrases, so I do not wait for the same words. I also wait until the speaker finishes the idea, because the first option mentioned is often a distractor.

89
00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:18.521
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:19.417 --> 00:06:25.622
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: listen for meaning, not just words.

91
00:06:25.922 --> 00:06:30.710
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

92
00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.500
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.219
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

